1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,820
Enemies in Returnal have

2
00:00:00,820 --> 00:00:03,360
tentacles that writhe as if alive.

3
00:00:03,360 --> 00:00:04,640
For this kind of effect, the developers used

4
00:00:04,640 --> 00:00:06,900
particles connected to one another.

5
00:00:06,900 --> 00:00:09,760
Connected points follow one another’s motion.

6
00:00:09,760 --> 00:00:13,520
Then we will build a thick surface around them.

7
00:00:13,520 --> 00:00:17,160
The initial approach attached a physical body to each bone.

8
00:00:17,160 --> 00:00:20,520
But computation cost and artistic control were difficult.

9
00:00:20,520 --> 00:00:25,160
The team developed the particle structure in a GPU effects tool.

10
00:00:25,160 --> 00:00:28,080
The points connect through parent and child relationships.

11
00:00:28,080 --> 00:00:30,180
Each child references one parent,

12
00:00:30,180 --> 00:00:33,240
while a parent can have multiple children.

13
00:00:33,240 --> 00:00:36,500
A child uses its parent’s information from one frame earlier.

14
00:00:36,500 --> 00:00:37,500
The parent moves first,

15
00:00:37,500 --> 00:00:39,380
and later points follow with a delay,

16
00:00:39,380 --> 00:00:41,480
producing organic motion.

17
00:00:41,480 --> 00:00:42,740
Moving points alone

18
00:00:42,740 --> 00:00:44,960
do not make a thick tentacle visible.

19
00:00:44,960 --> 00:00:48,600
The initial flat ribbons became cylindrical surfaces.

20
00:00:48,600 --> 00:00:51,440
Smooth curves are built along the points.

21
00:00:51,440 --> 00:00:53,240
Even from the side or in shadow,

22
00:00:53,240 --> 00:00:55,080
their volume remains readable.

23
00:00:55,080 --> 00:00:56,040
If the surface twists,

24
00:00:56,040 --> 00:00:58,280
its lighting can rotate strangely too.

25
00:00:58,280 --> 00:00:59,900
So the surface orientation

26
00:00:59,900 --> 00:01:01,920
is inherited and refined from the parent

27
00:01:01,920 --> 00:01:03,760
using an additional calculation.

28
00:01:03,760 --> 00:01:05,140
The motion-driving points

29
00:01:05,140 --> 00:01:09,280
and a stable surface built around them are both needed.

30
00:01:09,280 --> 00:01:10,020
This motion also connects to

31
00:01:10,020 --> 00:01:14,020
states such as an enemy preparing an attack.

32
00:01:14,020 --> 00:01:15,260
Artists and animators

33
00:01:15,260 --> 00:01:18,540
adjusted motion timing so attacks were easy to read.

34
00:01:18,540 --> 00:01:21,740
Particles follow the parent’s earlier movement.

35
00:01:21,740 --> 00:01:24,760
Together with the surrounding surface, they bring the tentacles to life.
